From: conda-forge
Subject: [PATCH] link pathops into the skia component

Skia's minimal configuration (is_official_build with the optional modules
disabled) does not pull in the :pathops source set, because nothing else left in
the trimmed-down component depends on it. Consumers of the public
include/pathops/SkPathOps.h header then fail to link.

Upstream carries no GN argument to request pathops on its own, so add it to the
component's dependencies unconditionally. This matches what fonttools/skia does
on its chrome/m143-no-deps branch:
https://github.com/fonttools/skia/commit/149648a8a767e4faafc9f4da753df46cadbcc33a

--- a/BUILD.gn
+++ b/BUILD.gn
@@ -1681,6 +1681,7 @@
     ":lasx",
     ":minify_sksl",
     ":ndk_images",
+    ":pathops",
     ":png_decode_rust",
     ":raw",
     ":skx",
